hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"477","It is narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Make things easy and do not make them difficult. Put people at ease and do not repel them.\"\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 477; Arabic Hadith: 477"
"478","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with them both, relates: \"Among the Children of Israel, a man was hosted as a guest, and there was a she-cat in the house. He said to it: 'O she-cat, do not hiss at our guest.' The kittens in her belly began to hiss. He mentioned this matter to his prophet, peace be upon him, who said: 'Her likeness is like that of this Ummah that will come after you, whose ignorant ones will overpower the scholars.'\"\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 478; Arabic Hadith: 478"
"479","It is narrated from the Mother of the Believers, ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \"I was riding a stubborn camel and began to strike it. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Be gentle, for gentleness adorns whatever it is found in, and it is stripped from whatever it is removed from, rendering it unsightly.'\"\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 479; Arabic Hadith: 479"
"480","It is narrated from Abū Naḍrah: \"There was a man from our tribe, called Jābir or Juwaybir. He related: 'During the caliphate of ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, I came to his presence for a need. I arrived in Madīnah at night, and when morning came, I went to him. I was an intelligent man and had an eloquent manner of speech. I began to speak of the vilification and contemptibility of the worldly life and established that it held no worth. Beside him was a white-haired man dressed in white garments. When I finished speaking, he said: \"All your words are correct, except your disparagement of the worldly life, which is misplaced. Do you know what the worldly life is? It is in this very world that lies the provision for reaching the Hereafter. It is in this world that are the deeds whose recompense will be received in the Hereafter.\" A man who possessed greater knowledge of the worldly life than I spoke to me about it, so I said: \"O Amīr al-Muʾminīn, who is this man sitting beside you?\" He said: \"He is the leader of the Muslims, Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, may Allah be pleased with him.\"'\"\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 480; Arabic Hadith: 480"
"481","It is narrated from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Boasting of one's seniority (in age or status) is a most evil deed.\"\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 481; Arabic Hadith: 481"
"482","Al-Ḥārith ibn Laqīṭ, may Allah have mercy upon him, relates: \"Among us were some people that when their mare gave birth to a foal, they would slaughter it, saying: 'What value has my life that I should ride upon it?' Then a letter from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, reached us, stating: 'Take care of the provision that Allah, the Most High, has given you, for indeed the Day of Resurrection is still far off.'\"\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 482; Arabic Hadith: 482"
"483","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \"Fear injustice. Injustice will appear as\ndarkness on the Day of Rising. Fear avarice. Avarice destroyed people before\nyou and led them to shed one another's blood and to make lawful what was\nunlawful for them.\""
"484","Jabir reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \"During the final days of my community there\nwill be distortion, slander and tyranny, and it will begin with people\nwho commit injustices.\""
